[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-EVENT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded independent input-edge processes
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall support up to 256 independently triggered processes, each with 1..16 distinct scalar top-input rising/falling edge controls. Each triggered process shall start from pre-commit state while observing its own isolated blocking updates in later statements. Nonblocking updates from the sampled input batch shall commit together. Auxiliary four-state inputs shall retain the scalar 0/1/X/Z edge table; the primary clock shall start known zero.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Baseline implementation and evidence: RtlDesign.EventEvaluation; runtime edge_event; docs/open-items-100.md, numbered cases 001..040 and primary-negedge startup regression. This requirement excludes generated clocks, arbitrary event expressions and general timed scheduling. Final regression rechecks baseline behavior after this batch.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlOpenItems100Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-HIER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded elaborated hierarchy
STATEMENT: The frontend shall normalize supported module instances and elaborated generate scopes, preserving source paths and sizing whole-word input/output connections with source expression signedness.
COMMENT: Baseline evidence: docs/open-items-100.md, cases 071..080 and hierarchical falling-clock alias integration. Inout, open and selected output connections remain outside this contract.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/uhdm/rtl_flatten.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlHierarchyTests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-WORD-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded signed and two-state words
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support its normalized signed/unsigned logic and bit word operators for widths 1..128, preserving four-state masks and coercing two-state storage at assignment boundaries.
COMMENT: Baseline qualification: docs/open-items-100.md; RtlSignedWideTests, RtlOperatorTests and two-state cases 061..070. This requirement covers the operator subset accepted by validation, not every SystemVerilog expression or type.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/rtl/runtime.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlSignedWideTests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-REPEAT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Constant bounded repetition
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support literal repeat counts 0..256 and reject expanded nested execution above its 20000-statement budget.
COMMENT: Baseline evidence: docs/open-items-100.md, cases 041..050 and nested-repeat budget regression. Runtime-controlled for/while loops remain open.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlOpenItems100Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-MEM-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fixed one-dimensional four-state memories
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support 1..256-word fixed four-state memories with nonnegative declared bounds through INT32_MAX, in either direction, with unknown reads and ignored writes for invalid or X/Z indices.
COMMENT: Baseline evidence: docs/open-items-100.md, cases 081..090 and runtime memory_index guards. VS-RTL-BLOCK-003 extends the assignment kinds supported by this storage contract.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/uhdm/rtl_flatten.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/rtl/runtime.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlOpenItems100Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-TIME-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General event and delay scheduling
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support a general timed event queue, arbitrary event expressions and delay scheduling.
COMMENT: Open backlog; this batch does not implement or verify this general requirement. Existing scalar top-input edge processing remains a bounded subset.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-COMB-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General combinational processes
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support always_comb processes with language-defined sensitivity and scheduling.
COMMENT: Open backlog; the existing continuous-assignment DAG is a separate bounded contract.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-PROC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General procedural constructs
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support initialization, runtime-controlled loops, functions and tasks.
COMMENT: Open backlog; constant repeat and supported sequential statements do not close this requirement.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-TYPE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Composite and broader scalar types
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support structures, unions, enums and additional scalar integer types.
COMMENT: Open backlog; supported signed/unsigned logic/bit words remain bounded to 128 bits.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-ARRAY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General array and container operations
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support multidimensional, queue, dynamic and associative array operations.
COMMENT: Open backlog; this batch only extends blocking writes to whole elements of existing fixed one-dimensional memories.
